CONFIDENCE: 97

I read "exactly one person between" as slot distance 2, which is the literal meaning. Let Finn be in slot f. Dev is before Finn and two slots from Elif (f+1), so Dev is in f−1. Cara is two slots from Dev and can't be in f+1, so Cara is in f−3 and Ivo in f−4. Ben must be at least f+4 to satisfy the Cara and Elif distance rules, which needs f ≤ 5. Ivo needs f ≥ 5, so f = 5. That leaves Ann in slot 3, Gus in 7 and Hana in 8, and Ben in 9. I checked all 16 constraints against this arrangement and each holds.
